  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "both_h",
   "x": 2030,
   "y": 1130,
   "text": "Rules that apply to BOTH providers",
   "fontSize": 20,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 589010,
   "versionNonce": 565864,
   "version": 1,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "originalText": "Rules that apply to BOTH providers",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "width": 408,
   "height": 25
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "both_t",
   "x": 2030,
   "y": 1180,
   "text": "1.  Verify the id_token on your server \u2014 signature, iss, aud, exp, nonce.\n2.  Match state (CSRF) and nonce (replay) from step 2.\n3.  Identify users by (iss, sub) \u2014 never by email alone.\n4.  Use PKCE even with a backend; mandatory for SPA / mobile.\n5.  Exchange the code server-side so client_secret stays secret.\n6.  Then mint YOUR OWN short-lived JWTs \u2014 don't reuse the provider's\n     access_token as your session.",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "strokeColor": "#374151",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 517199,
   "versionNonce": 237173,
   "version": 1,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "originalText": "1.  Verify the id_token on your server \u2014 signature, iss, aud, exp, nonce.\n2.  Match state (CSRF) and nonce (replay) from step 2.\n3.  Identify users by (iss, sub) \u2014 never by email alone.\n4.  Use PKCE even with a backend; mandatory for SPA / mobile.\n5.  Exchange the code server-side so client_secret stays secret.\n6.  Then mint YOUR OWN short-lived JWTs \u2014 don't reuse the provider's\n     access_token as your session.",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "width": 701,
   "height": 140
  },
